======================================================================
THE EDGE-CENTRIC FORMULA
======================================================================

For a FIXED arc position e = {0,1}:
  self_loops_via_e = # labeled T where flipping e preserves class
  edges_via_e = # distinct class pairs connected by flipping e

By S_n symmetry:
  SL_full = C(n,2) * self_loops_via_e
  Total non-SL transitions = C(n,2) * (2^m - self_loops_via_e)

The STABILIZER of arc {0,1} in S_n is S_2 x S_{n-2}:
  S_2 = swap vertices 0 and 1
  S_{n-2} = permute vertices {2,...,n-1}
  |Stab| = 2 * (n-2)!

By Burnside on the stabilizer:
  edges_via_e = (1/|Stab|) * sum_{sigma in Stab} Fix_pair(sigma)
  where Fix_pair(sigma) counts T with sigma(T)=T and [T]!=[T flip e]

This is a Burnside sum over S_2 x S_{n-2} instead of S_n.
|S_2 x S_{n-2}| = 2*(n-2)! which is MUCH smaller than n!.

For n=9: |Stab| = 2*7! = 10080 vs |S_9| = 362880.
The computation is 36x FASTER per arc position.
And there are only C(n,2) = 36 positions (all equivalent).
So edges_via_e determines everything!

